# deploy — example configuration
#
# deploy's `make env` writes federation.env from this file and keeps it in step
# (by hand: cp federation.env.example federation.env).
#
#   KEY=value     set per host
#   # KEY=value   optional; the value shown is the default
#
# Tags, on the line above a setting:
#   [required]          must be set on every host
#   [secret]            never printed; your value never follows the example
#   [shared: M [KEY]]   same value as member M (its KEY); make env fills it
#   [dev]               read only by the dev overlay (make up-dev)
# The Makefile includes federation.env (gitignored) when it exists.

# =============================================================================
# deploy
# =============================================================================

# --- Members ---

# Where the member repos live: relative to this Makefile, or an absolute path
# on the host. The default assumes the infra/ workspace layout (siblings).
# INFRA_ROOT=..

# Member directory names. Override one only if your host renames it; the name
# must still match the member's upstream repo name, since 'make clone' derives
# the clone URL from it.
# VLLM_DIR=vllm-service
# DATA_DIR=data-plane

# The observability plane (Prometheus, Grafana, Loki): a pulled-image member
# with a bespoke Makefile. Set it empty to run this host without it.
# OBS_DIR=obs-plane

# The edge gateway (Caddy and Authelia), the single production entry point: a
# pulled-image member with a bespoke Makefile. It comes up last, health-gated.
# Set it empty to run this host without the gateway.
# EDGE_DIR=edge-plane

# The first-party (common.mk) apps this host runs, space-separated directory
# names. Trim it to the subset this host runs. Only common.mk apps belong
# here; open-webui-service has its own variable below.
# APP_DIRS=docint Nextext translator

# The upstream chat UI (pulled image, bespoke Makefile). It is kept out of
# APP_DIRS because it is a different kind of member, not because it is
# excluded: it joins every app-tier loop (setup, up, down, ps, logs) and the
# bundle and load fan-out. Set it empty to drop it from the federation.
# OPENWEBUI_DIR=open-webui-service

# The data-plane Qdrant profile: cpu or cuda.
# DATA_PROFILE=cpu

# --- Clone ---

# Where 'make clone' fetches the members from: an account or namespace PREFIX,
# not a full URL. Each member is cloned from $GIT_REMOTE/<dir>.git. Over SSH:
#   GIT_REMOTE=git@github.com:nos-tromo
# From an internal mirror:
#   GIT_REMOTE=https://git.example.internal/mirror/nos-tromo
# GIT_REMOTE=https://github.com/nos-tromo

# --- Health gates ---

# How long a health gate waits for a tier, in seconds (wait-healthy.sh).
# WAIT_TIMEOUT=180

# The image tag the health-probe container runs. Override WAIT_PROBE_IMAGE and
# WAIT_PROBE_PIN together if you swap the probe image.
# WAIT_PROBE_IMAGE=busybox:1.37

# The digest-pinned reference 'make bundle' pulls and saves for the airgap
# host. The pin must be a digest of the image WAIT_PROBE_IMAGE names.
# WAIT_PROBE_PIN=busybox@sha256:9db7b59979c38555a39def84a31fb98b5296952f9e3afd4f6f11f05b07adfab0

# --- One-shot switches ---

# Each is usually passed on the command line instead, for one run only.

# 1 = 'make bundle' rebuilds every member even when its bundle for the
# current release tag exists (judged by the member's .<slug>-version file; see
# scripts/bundle-exists.sh). One run: make bundle BUNDLE_FORCE=1
# BUNDLE_FORCE=

# 1 = 'make prune' also removes the unused versions of the upstream images
# the members pull (qdrant, grafana, ...); by default it removes only the
# images the federation builds. Upstream images match by repository, so an
# unused image of the same repository pulled by another project on this host
# goes too. One run: make prune PRUNE_UPSTREAM=1
# PRUNE_UPSTREAM=

# 1 = 'make env' also generates the shared secrets that are unset in every
# member (a missing value is otherwise left for you to fill in). One run:
# make env ENV_GENERATE=1
# ENV_GENERATE=

# 1 = let 'make up' and 'make up-dev' go ahead while a .env is behind its
# example (env-check otherwise stops the bring-up before any tier). One run:
# make up ENV_ALLOW_DRIFT=1
# ENV_ALLOW_DRIFT=
